      "seed": 2,
      "version": 20,
      "versionNonce": 236159300,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791461244024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Factory Pattern: put object-creation choices in one place. The rest of the program asks for a vehicle and uses it through a common interface.\nLayman: tell the garage “I need a truck”; the garage picks and hands you the right vehicle. You drive it without building it yourself.\nThis lesson uses a Simple Factory (a common beginner technique), not the GoF Factory Method pattern.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Factory Pattern: put object-creation choices in one place. The rest of the program asks for a vehicle and uses it through a common interface.\nLayman: tell the garage “I need a truck”; the garage picks and hands you the right vehicle. You drive it without building it yourself.\nThis lesson uses a Simple Factory (a common beginner technique), not the GoF Factory Method pattern.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a1"
    },
    {
