    {
      "id": "factory-problem-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 105,
      "y": 245,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 4,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1015438972,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791461068249,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WITHOUT A FACTORY\n\nA client constructs concrete classes itself:\na = new Car()\nb = new Truck()\nc = new Bike()\n\nIf many parts of the program create vehicles,\nthey all need to know the concrete class names.\nWhen choice is dynamic, each may repeat the\nCar / Truck / Bike if-else decision.",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 18,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WITHOUT A FACTORY\n\nA client constructs concrete classes itself:\na = new Car()\nb = new Truck()\nc = new Bike()\n\nIf many parts of the program create vehicles,\nthey all need to know the concrete class names.\nWhen choice is dynamic, each may repeat the\nCar / Truck / Bike if-else decision.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a3"
    },
